The comment states "nodesToCheck already excludes nodes with pods (filtered by managedNodes)" but this is misleading. The managedNodes set contains nodes that are in the ClusterUpgradeState.NodeStates, which represents nodes actively managed by the upgrade process. This doesn't necessarily mean "nodes with pods" - it means "nodes currently tracked in the upgrade state machine". 

A node could have a driver pod running but not be in the upgrade state if the state hasn't been built yet or if there are other conditions. The comment should more accurately describe what managedNodes represents to avoid confusion.
